 <a name="implicit-code-systems"> </a>
 <h2>Implicit Code Systems</h2>
 <p>
-Some other parts of the FHIR infrastructure define set of concepts that may also be treated as code systems. This is most useful when mapping between systems using <a title="[%resdesc ConceptMap%]" href="conceptmap.html">Concept Maps</a>, but might also be useful for other code system related functionality (e.g. subsetting using <a title="[%resdesc ValueSet%]" href="valueset.html">Value Sets</a>). The table below summarizes how to treat these items as a code system:
+Instead of an explicit code system definition (e.g., a FHIR CodeSystem instance), implicit CodeSystems can be inferred from an instance of each of the Resources below. The value of various CodeSystem elements is inferred from elements in the corresponding resources based on the mapping table below. Such code systems are particularly useful when mapping between the underpinning structures in the table below using <a title="[%resdesc ConceptMap%]" href="conceptmap.html">Concept Maps</a>. The table below summarizes how to treat these items as a code system:
 </p>
 <table class="grid">
+   <tr>
+     <th>Implicit Code System Resource Type</th>
+     <th>Code System Element</th>
+     <th>Implicit Code System Resource Type Source Element</th>
+   </tr>
  <!-- StructureDefinition -->
    <tr>
    <td rowspan="5"><b><a title="[%resdesc StructureDefinition%]" href="structuredefinition.html">StructureDefinition</a></b></td>
